 "result": "Call order at the end of a request:\n\n1. `Tessel.wsgi_entry` — `src/tessel/app.py` (~L1566)\n2. `Tessel.run_full_request` — `src/tessel/app.py`\n3. `Tessel.finalize_request` — `src/tessel/app.py` (calls `make_response`, then `finalize_reply`)\n4. `Tessel.finalize_reply` — `src/tessel/app.py` (~L1394). It runs the `after_request` funcs, then calls `persist_session` unless the session is a null session.\n5. `SessionInterface.persist_session` — `src/tessel/sessions.py`, implemented by `SignedCookieSessionInterface`:\n   - empty and modified → `response.delete_cookie`\n   - empty and unmodified → nothing\n   - otherwise, if `cookie_needs_write` is true (modified, or permanent with `SESSION_REFRESH_EACH_REQUEST`) → `response.set_cookie`\n6. Inside that `set_cookie` branch:\n   - `get_cookie_name/domain/path/httponly/secure/samesite/partitioned` supply the cookie options.\n   - `get_expiration_time` supplies the expiry.\n   - `make_signer(app)` builds the signer.\n   - `TypedCookieSerializer` (`session_json_serializer`, `src/tessel/json/tag.py`) encodes the payload.\n\nThe cookie is then sent with the response returned by `response(environ, start_response)`.\n\nI took this from `brain/sessions.md` and `brain/request-lifecycle.md` and did not open the source files.",
